This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on 
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1] Applying a crysknife to a tiger-eye ring cuts the gem off the 
ring, so that it no longer has an eye; and "ring" without "i" is 
"RNG", so this should cause a random bad event to happen.

[2] Scroll of dyslexia. When read, turns your god into a dog for a few 
hundred turns, so that he can no longer give artifact gifts and only 
barks angrily if you transgress.

[3] Eucalyptus golem. When killed, leaves a pile of 2d6 eucalyptus 
leaves.

[4] Magnet. When applied in a direction, pulls any magnetic metal 
items one or two squares towards the wielder, such as iron chains, 
iron balls, certain types of armour, and smaller monsters that are 
wearing such things. Good for luring iron golems down holes.

[5] Chocolate golem. Highly susceptible to fire attacks: one 
successful hit will melt it, leaving a gooey mess that solidifies into 
a candy bar after approximately 50 turns (or faster if placed on an 
ice square or in an ice box).

[6] Ice-cream van. This is like a #rideable creature, but you drive 
around in it serving cream pies from its built-in ice box. Any monster 
in a two-square radius can be given a chilled cream pie to be tamed. 
If cursed, the monster demands a refund and you lose some gold. Better 
chance of attracting monsters if you are carrying a musical instrument 
and can play Greensleeves. Note that "cold" monsters (such as winter 
wolves) are not interested in ice-cream.




